  "body": "## What changed\n\nA new built-in post **LinuxCNC** (`assets/posts/linuxcnc.cps`, extension `.ngc`) and a generic machine **LinuxCNC 3-axis** (`assets/machines/linuxcnc-3axis.mch`). The post uses the RS274NGC dialect from the public LinuxCNC 2.9 G-code and M-code references. Its structure comes from our own `tormach.cps`. The PathPilot assumptions are removed: no \"machine Z0 is the top\" convention, no G30 before each tool change, no belt-range notes, no 1-1000 tool range, no 4th axis.\n\nPost options (declared, so the UI, CLI and MCP show them):\n\n| Option | Values | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| `retractMode` | `g53` (`G53 G0 Z<safe_retract>`), `g28` / `g30` (`G91 G28 Z0` + `G90`, Z only), `none` | `g53` |\n| `writeToolLength` | `G43 H<n>` after `T<n> M6`; off when the M6 remap applies the length (the section `G49` is then left out too) | on |\n| `pathControl` / `blendTolerance` | `G64 P<tol>` (mm, written in the program unit) or `G61` | `G64 P0.025` |\n| `programEnd` | `M30` or `M2` | `M30` |\n| `percentDelimiters` | `%` on the first and the last line | off |\n\nAlso: safe start block `G21|G20 G17 G90 G91.1 G94 G40 G49 G80`, no O word, comments in parentheses (active keywords made inert), `S M3`, `M7`/`M8`/`M9` from the machine coolant list (`PARAM Coolant` read), arcs and helices with incremental IJK (or the R-arc option), G73/G81/G82/G83/G85/G86/G89 with G99, G38.2/G38.3 probing as in the PathPilot post.\n\nBase: upstream main `fac6c8e8d` (not a cut tag: the fork main is behind v0.22.0, and this PR targets upstream main).\n\nTapping:\n- A rigid tap is `G33.1 Z<bottom> K<pitch>` (pitch = feed / rpm). The post writes it only when the machine file states `rigid_tapping: true` (the reference requires a spindle encoder). Else it refuses by name.\n- A floating-holder tap is `G84 ... F<rpm x pitch>` (the reference says G84 is not spindle-synchronized). The post declares `floatingTapping = true`.\n\nRefused by name: `G53` retract with no stated `safe_retract` (no machine included, #435 / #495), control compensation (G41/G42), tilted moves, a trip home after an operation, tool numbers that are not positive whole numbers, G73/G83 with Q <= 0.\n\nEngine: the machine mirror read an unstated `rigid_tapping` as `rigidTapping: true` (the unstated-limit law). The post must not take that as \"an encoder is present\". So the engine now also publishes `machine.rigidTappingStated` (true only for a stated `rigid_tapping: true`). No other post reads it. `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` documents it.\n\nRegistration: `BUILTINS` and `MACHINES` (`crates/app/src/posting.rs`), the post-name lists in `cam.d.ts` and `script/mod.rs`, README, `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`. Decisions: `docs/decisions/2303-linuxcnc-post.md`.\n\n## How it was tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `crates/app/tests/linuxcnc_post.rs` (9 tests): registry and library; unstated safe Z refused, never `G53 G0 Z0`; stated safe Z before `M6`, after `G43` and at the end; `G28`/`G30`/none retracts; no `G43`/section `G49` with the remap option; `G61`, `M2`, `%`, inch blend tolerance, end units; rigid tap refused without an encoder and `G33.1 Z-12 K1.5` with one (inch `K0.059055`); floating tap `G84`; tilted move and control compensation refused. Every program is checked to hold only G/M words from the LinuxCNC reference.\n- `conformance`: new goldens `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/*.nc` (12) and `synth_linuxcnc.nc`; `tap_plate` is a named refusal on the generic VMC (no encoder stated); extension `.ngc` pinned.\n- `script_linuxcnc` (post binary on the recorded streams, goldens in `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/linuxcnc/`). These are machine-less, so each case is the named safe-Z refusal (or the 3-axis refusal).\n- Cross-post lists extended: `cycle_hop` (hop law, run with `retractMode=g30`), `ream_cycle`, `comp`, `control_comp`, `wear_comp`, `post_spindle_rule_all`, `machine`.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, head 95b83ca24, macOS): 579 steps, 573 green. The 6 red suites are exactly the 18 tests that #2306 lists as red on this base (`fac6c8e8d`, main is red after batch 16): `circular_pick_law`, `keep_law`, `kept_parts_live`, `pocket3d_open_side`, `stock_source_holes`, `trochoid_law`. None of them posts through this post.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` and clippy on the new and changed app test targets: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Not run in a LinuxCNC sim or on a machine. The reporter (sn3ro) offered a LinuxCNC 2.9 sim run and an air cut.\n- G33.1 and G84 behaviour on a real spindle; the `none` retract with a real M6 remap.\n- Control compensation (G41/G42) is refused, not written. A 4th axis is not supported.\n\nChangelog: New LinuxCNC 3-axis mill post and generic machine: retract by G53 safe Z, G28/G30 or none; optional G43 after a remapped M6; G64 P or G61; G33.1 rigid tap only with a stated spindle encoder, G84 for floating holders (#2303)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #2303\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
